  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "1rmvX6IeqaqIYKez9VbriKMZV/M=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:14.449Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## Installable, and offline by default\n\nConnect is a PWA: users can install it, and a precaching **service worker** keeps the app shell available offline \u2014 along with its in-browser database assets and registry-loaded editors. It is built on `vite-plugin-pwa` and Workbox, configured entirely through `powerhouse.config.json` rather than a separate PWA config file.\n\nOffline support is on by default via `connect.app.offline`:\n\n```bash\nph connect config connect.app.offline false\nph connect build --json '{\"app\":{\"offline\":false}}'\n```\n\n## Three behaviours worth knowing\n\n**The worker is production-only.** During local development it is always disabled regardless of `connect.app.offline`, so hot-reload is never intercepted by a cache. A caching bug you cannot reproduce in `ph connect studio` is expected.\n\n**Disabling is not a no-op \u2014 it emits a self-destroying worker.** Any worker installed by an earlier build unregisters itself and clears its caches on the browser's next update check. That matters because a service worker outlives the deploy that installed it: without the tombstone, users who visited the offline-enabled build would keep serving stale assets forever.\n\n**Workbox runs in `injectManifest` mode with a hand-written worker.** Connect owns the worker source; your `globPatterns` feed the injected precache list, and your `runtimeCaching` rules are registered by that worker *after* its built-ins. Workbox is first-match-wins, and the built-ins (Google Fonts, the `/-/cdn/` registry assets, `powerhouse.config.json`) are registered first \u2014 so custom rules add coverage but cannot override a built-in rule for the same URL. A `urlPattern` is either a verbatim string or `{ source, flags }` rebuilt into a `RegExp`; function patterns are not supported. For `NetworkFirst`, set `options.networkTimeoutSeconds` or a slow network stalls instead of falling back to cache.\n\n`connect.pwa` is validated at build time and only applies when `offline` is `true`; an unknown field, bad file handler or non-compiling regex fails `ph connect build` naming the offending field. It is build-time only \u2014 set it with `ph connect build`, not `ph connect config`, which writes the file but cannot rebuild the worker.\n\n_Source: `apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/05-Launch/06-ConfigurePWA.md`, Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:37:13.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:37:14.449Z"
    }
  },
